      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-bellica-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<ul><li>Wild-caught Betta bellica from Malaysia, from the Betta bellica complex.</li><li>IUCN Red List: Least Concern.</li><li>Max size: 10 cm (4 inches)</li><li>TDS: 60–100</li><li>pH: 5.0–6.5</li><li>Temperature: 24–28°C (75–82°F)</li><li>Breeding: bubble nest builder</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-bellica-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Fed live blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-bellica-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Their behaviour was found to be similar to the Unimaculata complex. Although some sites describe them as fairly peaceful, they have been on the more aggressive side. Treat them like Betta splendens.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-bellica-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Males have better coloring and pointier dorsal and caudal fins than females.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-bellica-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>Bubble nest builder.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/betta-bellica-wild-betta-fish",
      "html": "<p>This species has a green iridescent body with long fins. Males have better coloring, especially while breeding. Males have a pointier dorsal fin, caudal fin and tail than females. This is the largest bubble-nesting betta, with a temperament similar to Betta unimaculata.</p>"
    }
